  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jamshed vs State Of Rajasthan Through Pp on 3 January, 2018",
    "facts": "Petitioner has filed this miscellaneous bail application under Section 438 Cr.P.C. 2. F.I.R. No.217/2017 was registered at Police Station Kaman, District Bharatpur for offence under Sections 420, 272 of I.P.C. and Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "3. It is contended by counsel for the petitioner that offences under Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 as well as offences under Sections 272 of IPC are bailable and Section 420 of IPC has been added to make it a non-bailable offence.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. It is contended by counsel for the petitioner that offences under Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 as well as offences under Sections 272 of IPC are bailable and Section 420 of IPC has been added to make it a non-bailable offence.",
